MAXUSAI 905: restore RESIZE_ALGO_BILINEAR for gemma4 and qwen3vl.

b10864 changed the vision resampler for these projectors in the same hunk that
raised gemma4's token ceiling from (40,280) to (70,1120):

    -   hparams.image_resize_algo = RESIZE_ALGO_BILINEAR;
    +   hparams.image_resize_algo = RESIZE_ALGO_BICUBIC;
    -   hparams.set_limit_image_tokens(40, 280);
    +   hparams.set_limit_image_tokens(70, 1120);

Separately, the naive resamplers (resize_bilinear, resize_bicubic) were deleted
and every algo now routes through the Pillow-parity path, so BICUBIC also means
something different than it did: antialiased, with half-pixel centres.

MEASURED ON gfx1151 (Radeon 8060S), gemma4:31b-it-q4_K_M, budget pinned via
run_budget_sweep.sh, name_bbox_mean_iou (vertical localization):

    budget   0.32.1/b9888   0.34.1/b10864
       280       0.612          0.691
       560       0.713          0.714
      1120       0.728          0.000     <-- total loss

The grid is unchanged: prompt_eval_count is identical between builds on every
test (1684 on scene_single), so the token count and tokenization are the same
and only the PIXELS differ. The failure is confined to the 1120 rung, which is
the only rung that enlarges a 1920x1080 source (1120 * 48^2 = 2580480 px), and
it is the vertical axis that breaks -- the same axis and the same rung as the
coordinate defect ADR 0007 mitigated and ADR 0008 declared fixed by patch 004.
